From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:09:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] store: build without if-let guards for Rust 1.94

Thread::try_from binds the service id of a CallEvent sync message in an
`if let` match guard (#471). Rust 1.94, which oe-core wrynose ships,
rejects that: "`if let` guards are experimental" (E0658). Check the
parse in a plain guard and parse again in the arm instead; the match
falls through to the "any other message" arm exactly as before when the
conversation id is no service id.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [toolchain compatibility: oe-core wrynose has Rust 1.94]
---
 presage/src/store.rs | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/presage/src/store.rs b/presage/src/store.rs
index 784164454..5646f6daf 100644
--- a/presage/src/store.rs
+++ b/presage/src/store.rs
@@ -527,8 +527,12 @@ impl TryFrom<&Content> for Thread {
                         ..
                     })),
                 ..
-            }) if let Some(service_id) = ServiceId::parse_from_service_id_binary(conversation_id) => {
-                Ok(Self::Contact(service_id))
+            }) if ServiceId::parse_from_service_id_binary(conversation_id).is_some() => {
+                // Parsed again rather than bound in an `if let` guard, which Rust 1.94 rejects.
+                Ok(Self::Contact(
+                    ServiceId::parse_from_service_id_binary(conversation_id)
+                        .expect("checked by the match guard"),
+                ))
             }
             // [1-1] Any other message directly to us
             _ => Ok(Thread::Contact(content.metadata.sender)),
